# catppuccin — Catppuccin Mocha, mapped onto Ergon's 22 roles.
#
# NOT derived from a matplotlib colormap, unlike cool/winter/spring/summer/
# autumn/plasma. This is an established scheme with its own published palette,
# reproduced here under its licence; see theme/LICENSES.md.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/catppuccin/palette (palette.json, v1.8.0)
# Licence:  MIT, Copyright (c) 2021 Catppuccin
#
# Mocha is the darkest of the four flavours. Every value below is upstream's,
# verified character-for-character against palette.json; nothing is invented.
# The MAPPING is ours -- Catppuccin publishes 26 names and Ergon needs 22 roles.

# -- neutrals ---------------------------------------------------------------
COOL_BG0=#1E1E2E          # base
COOL_BG1=#313244          # surface0
COOL_BG2=#45475A          # surface1
COOL_FG0=#CDD6F4          # text
COOL_FG1=#BAC2DE          # subtext1
COOL_DIM=#A6ADC8          # subtext0
COOL_DIMMER=#9399B2       # overlay2
# -- the ramp: teal -> sky -> blue -> mauve -> pink -------------------------
COOL_0=#94E2D5
COOL_1=#89DCEB
COOL_2=#89B4FA
COOL_3=#CBA6F7
COOL_4=#F5C2E7
# -- alert pair -------------------------------------------------------------
COOL_HOT_0=#74C7EC        # sapphire
COOL_HOT_4=#F38BA8        # red
# -- off-ramp tints ---------------------------------------------------------
COOL_MINT=#A6E3A1         # green
COOL_BLUSH=#F5E0DC        # rosewater
# -- semantic aliases -------------------------------------------------------
# Unlike cool, the alert roles use the scheme's OWN semantic colours: a palette
# that publishes a red should not signal danger in magenta.
COOL_ACCENT=#89B4FA       # blue
COOL_ACTIVE=#CBA6F7       # mauve, Mocha's signature accent
COOL_URGENT=#F38BA8       # red
COOL_WARN=#F9E2AF         # yellow
COOL_GOOD=#A6E3A1         # green
COOL_INACTIVE=#45475A     # surface1
